      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "<p>Pum[bedita], and by our master, Tsadok, head of the academy in the city of Me\u1e25asya [Sura]; and our master Na\u1e25shon, gaon of Me\u1e25asya [from 810 to 812]; his son; and his brother, Mar Rav Moses, my maternal grandfather. Their questions attest to their deep understanding and great wisdom, because wisdom is a fortress to the wise, stronger than ten rulers, and the good name that becomes ascribed to them is theirs forever, as it is written: O that my words were written down; would they were inscribed in a record, incised on a rock forever, with iron stylus and lead! (Job 19:23\u201324).</p>\n<p>And after our masters Tsema\u1e25 and Tov were gathered to Eden, no questions from you arrived. This was in the days of our master and teacher Yehudah Ga\u2019on [from 905 to 917], and he along with our master and teacher Mishoy [ben Isaac Tsadok] alluf [an honorific] were scribes at the gate of our master Tsema\u1e25, my paternal great-grandfather, may they rest in peace. Afterwards, questions arrived from your locales for our master Kohen Tsedek Ga\u2019on [from 917 to 935], of blessed memory.</p>\n<p>O you, light of my eyes, and the people of your region,</p>",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
